{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T17:17:57.100Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b76020648d06f21575f92b8e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-wlxf8f","claim:pm-y26mvc","lineage:pm-wlxf8f","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-wlxf8f+pm-y26mvc","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-wlxf8f","claim:pm-y26mvc","lineage:pm-wlxf8f","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-1du7s3"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Unknown-option refusals on extension commands with declared flags carry code unknown_option and list only the flags the command accepts"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Shippable tranche of pm-4of199 (2026-11-07). On an extension-created command that declares flags, an undeclared option was refused with an untyped command_failed and a list of every host definition it is validated against, including --no-extensions and, on a non-read command, the read-output controls the command refuses. The refusal now carries code unknown_option with the refused flag, and lists the command's declared flags followed by the host flags it inherits, from the same declaration pm contracts publishes as inherited_flags. The dynamic-dispatch refusal for a command without declared flags gets the same code and host-flag list. Refusing undeclared options on a zero-flag command's handler path is NOT part of this tranche: a census of the package fleet found released packages that read options they never declare, so that flip stays on pm-4of199 behind the fleet migration item."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","extensions","flags","validation"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-07T17:17:57.100Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T17:17:57.100Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm <ext-cmd> --bogus on a command with declared flags exits 2 with code unknown_option and flag --bogus; The refusal lists the declared flags, then the inherited host flags, never --no-extensions, and read-output controls only on a command that declares read_output; The dynamic-dispatch zero-flag refusal carries the same code and host-flag list; A built-CLI integration spec covers a non-read and a read_output command"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-4of199"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"37ec8d7e7a087bd25509a6fd7be123e780c86e4864673046a1b7762da4ab53ef","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0d641792193fa4d5182525f8edd5e5a37f3b64b5c51d8b7e191d63e1a4c65a0a"}
